            targetName +
            " learner keeps making one mistake. Name the grammar point it belongs to, for a label they read mid-call, and say in one short sentence what to watch for.\n\nFirst decide: is it a GRAMMAR point (a form, an ending, word order, an article, a particle, a tense — a rule that applies to other words too), or a WORD choice (one word or name confused with another, a collocation)? Set \"grammar\" to true or false.\n\nReturn {\"grammar\": true, \"label\": \"...\", \"tip\": \"...\"}, label and tip in " +
            nativeName +
            ":\n- label: the grammar point as a learner would say it, 2–4 words   (e.g. \"past tense\", \"articles a/the\", \"subject particle\"). Not   the example, not a sentence.\n- tip: one plain sentence, at most 12 words, about WHEN it applies.   Friendly, never scolding, no grammar jargon beyond the label."

